      "writtenOn": "2026-09-18T14:10:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We typically add a define to Chromium\u0027s skia/config/SkUserConfig.h file to preserve the old behavior, then land a Skia change that relies on the define, then update Chromium to opt into the new behavior.\n\nThis can either be add a SK_USE_LEGACY_FOO flag to chrome\u0027s SkUserConfig.h file, wrap all the new code in skia in a `#if !defined(SK_USE_LEGACY_FOO)`, roll Skia into chrome, then remove the SK_USE_LEGACY_FOO change from chrome with additional changes as required to use new behavior, then clean up #defines back in Skia when no one uses SK_USE_LEGACY_FOO.\n\nOR \n\nWrap all the new code in skia in a `#if defined(SK_ENABLE_NEW_FOO)`, roll skia into chrome, update chrome\u0027s SKUserConfig.h to define SK_ENABLE_NEW_FOO plus required code changes, then clean up #defines in Skia when everyone uses SK_ENABLE_NEW_FOO, then remove now unused SK_ENABLE_NEW_FOO from chrome\u0027s SkUserConfig.h",
      "parentUuid": "3d9345c1_0597584e",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 73,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 73,
        "endChar": 14
      },
